---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="Privacy Policy" description="How domkirby.com handles information collected through its forms, analytics, and bot protection.">
  <!-- data-pagefind-body: index this page's own content, not the site chrome -->
  <section class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-16" data-pagefind-body>
    <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold text-white mb-2">domkirby.com Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="text-white/60 mb-10"><strong class="text-white">Effective date:</strong> October 14, 2026</p>

    <div class="prose prose-invert prose-lg max-w-none
      prose-headings:text-white
      prose-a:text-green prose-a:hover:underline
      prose-strong:text-white
      prose-th:text-white
    ">
      <p>
        This site collects only what you type into a form, uses it only to answer that form, measures traffic with
        privacy-preserving analytics, and uses Cloudflare Turnstile to keep bots out of its forms. We do not sell your information.
      </p>

      <h2>Who we are</h2>
      <p>
        This Privacy Policy explains how Dom Kirby Creative, LLC ("we," "us," or "our") handles information collected through
        domkirby.com (the "Site"). We are based in Colorado, United States.
      </p>

      <h2>Information you give us</h2>
      <p>
        The only personal information we collect is what you choose to enter into a form on the Site, such as a speaking
        inquiry or contact form. Depending on the form, this may include:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Your name and email address</li>
        <li>Your organization, role, or event details</li>
        <li>The content of your message</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        We use form information only for the purpose that form exists. A speaking inquiry is used to respond about speaking;
        a contact message is used to reply to you. We do not add you to a mailing list or use your submission for marketing
        unless you ask us to.
      </p>
      <p>We do not ask for sensitive information through the Site. Please do not send it.</p>

      <h2>Analytics</h2>
      <p>
        We use two analytics tools to understand how the Site is used in aggregate, such as which pages are popular and how
        visitors find us. We do not use analytics to identify you personally.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Google Analytics via Cloudflare Zaraz.</strong> Google Analytics is loaded through Cloudflare Zaraz, which runs
        on Cloudflare's servers rather than in your browser. Zaraz anonymizes data before it reaches Google, including removing
        or truncating your IP address. Google receives aggregate usage data, not information that identifies you. Learn more in
        <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google's privacy policy</a>.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Plausible Analytics.</strong> We also use
        <a href="https://plausible.io/data-policy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Plausible Analytics</a>, a
        privacy-focused analytics platform that we operate ourselves. Plausible uses no cookies and does not store IP addresses
        or build visitor profiles. It records page views and general usage, such as pages visited, referring site, country or
        region, device and browser type. This data stays with us and is not shared with or sold to third parties.
      </p>
      <p>
        Plausible sets no cookies. Google Analytics via Zaraz may use cookies or similar technologies. You can block or delete
        cookies in your browser settings, and the Site works without them.
      </p>

      <h2>Bot protection (Cloudflare Turnstile)</h2>
      <p>
        Our forms are protected by
        <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/products/turnstile/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Cloudflare Turnstile</a>,
        a privacy-focused tool that tells human visitors apart from bots and blocks spam and abuse.
      </p>
      <p>
        To do this, Turnstile processes technical signals from your browser, such as your IP address, TLS fingerprint,
        user-agent, and the site you are visiting. These signals are not used to identify, profile, or target you. Cloudflare
        processes them on our behalf to secure this Site, and also uses them as a controller to improve Turnstile's bot detection.
      </p>
      <p>
        Cloudflare's processing of this data is described in the
        <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/turnstile-privacy-policy/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Turnstile Privacy Addendum</a>
        and the
        <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Cloudflare Privacy Policy</a>.
        For requests about data processed to protect this Site, contact us. For questions about Cloudflare's own use of
        Turnstile data, contact Cloudflare's Data Protection Officer at
        <a href="mailto:dpo@cloudflare.com">dpo@cloudflare.com</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>How we use and share information</h2>
      <p>We use information only to respond to your form submission, operate and secure the Site, and understand aggregate traffic.</p>
      <p>
        We do <strong>not</strong> sell your personal information. We do <strong>not</strong> share it for targeted advertising.
        We do <strong>not</strong> use it for profiling or automated decisions about you.
      </p>
      <p>
        We may disclose information if required by law, to protect our rights or the safety of others, or in connection with a
        business transfer such as a merger. In a transfer, this policy's commitments would continue to apply to your information.
      </p>

      <h2>Service providers</h2>
      <p>
        We rely on a small number of providers to run the Site. They process information only on our behalf and under their own
        privacy and security commitments.
      </p>
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr><th>Provider</th><th>What they do</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>Cloudflare</td><td>Hosting, security, content delivery, Zaraz tag management, and Turnstile bot protection</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Google</td><td>Anonymized, aggregate analytics via Zaraz</td></tr>
          <tr><td>HubSpot</td><td>CRM that may receive and store form submissions so we can respond</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>

      <h2>Retention and security</h2>
      <p>
        We keep form submissions only as long as needed to respond and to maintain a reasonable record of our correspondence,
        then delete them. You can ask us to delete yours sooner. Analytics data is kept in aggregate or anonymized form.
      </p>
      <p>
        We use reasonable technical and organizational safeguards, including encrypted connections (HTTPS) and access controls
        on the systems that hold your information. No system is perfectly secure. If a breach affecting your personal
        information occurs, we will notify you as required by Colorado law.
      </p>

      <h2>Your choices and rights</h2>
      <p>Wherever you live, you can contact us to:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Access the personal information we hold about you</li>
        <li>Correct inaccurate information</li>
        <li>Delete your information</li>
        <li>Get a copy of your information in a portable format</li>
      </ul>
      <p>We respond within 45 days. We will not treat you differently for making a request.</p>
      <p>
        <strong>Colorado residents.</strong> The Colorado Privacy Act gives Colorado consumers rights to access, correct, delete,
        and port their data, and to opt out of sale, targeted advertising, and profiling. We do not sell personal data or use it
        for targeted advertising or profiling, so there is nothing to opt out of. We honor these rights requests regardless. If
        we deny a request, you may appeal by replying to our decision; if you remain unsatisfied, you may contact the
        <a href="https://coag.gov/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Colorado Attorney General</a>.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Global Privacy Control.</strong> We honor browser-based opt-out signals such as Global Privacy Control (GPC).
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Blocking analytics.</strong> You can block cookies, use a content blocker, or use Google's
        <a href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">opt-out browser add-on</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Children</h2>
      <p>
        The Site is intended for adults and business audiences. We do not knowingly collect personal information from anyone
        under 18. If you believe a minor has submitted information, contact us and we will delete it.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
      <p>
        We may update this policy. When we do, we will change the effective date above. Material changes will be noted on this page.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Questions or requests about your privacy: <a href="mailto:security@domkirby.com">security@domkirby.com</a>.
      </p>
      <p>Dom Kirby Creative, LLC<br />Colorado, United States</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
